# Engineering Guardrails

1. All development happens inside `/home/jro/asb-product-work`.
2. Product work uses isolated candidate branches/worktrees; never edit `main`.
3. No development process may access home, vault, real notes, real inbox data,
   databases, credentials, `.env` files, runtime state, or home services.
4. Never merge a candidate into the isolated product integration line without
   an explicit owner decision. Never deploy, activate, restart services, sync
   remotes, or promote work to home without a separate explicit owner release
   decision.
5. Keep every package within approved paths and its stated product scope.
6. Run deterministic tests and preserve true command/exit results.
7. Ordinary defects are repaired within the package budget; do not ask the
   owner for routine retry approval.
8. Candidate verification and any required independent review happen against
   one frozen candidate SHA. Agent C verifies first; the independent reviewer
   runs only afterward and never concurrently with Agent C.
9. Preserve evidence and the candidate branch on a hard stop.
10. Do not create delivery/orchestration tooling unless the owner explicitly
    reopens that work after a product release.
